{"type":"message","id":"b11f1223","parentId":"5266af0b","timestamp":"2026-02-10T16:35:00.730Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[cron:e30c88a4-9e5a-4969-9b03-0b072e949607 Bourse EU - Fermeture] Recherche les cours de bourse européens à la clôture et fais un récap complet.\n\n⚠️ Robustesse source (obligatoire):\n- N'utilise pas Yahoo seul.\n- Si Yahoo échoue (404/erreur), passe en multi-source.\n- Utilise au moins 2 sources parmi: Euronext, Investing, MarketWatch, CNBC, TradingView, Stooq.\n- Ne bloque pas le rapport si une source tombe.\n\nContenu:\n1) Indices: CAC 40, DAX, Euro Stoxx 50, FTSE 100 (cours + variation + bilan jour)\n2) Principales actions: top 5 hausses / top 5 baisses du CAC 40 et du DAX + blue chips (LVMH, TotalEnergies, SAP, ASML, Siemens, etc.)\n3) Actions à surveiller pour demain: after-hours, résultats attendus, événements macro\n4) Michelin (MFP): cours clôture, variation jour, valeur des 111 actions\n\nFormat: emojis + bullet points, sans tableau markdown.\nSi donnée absente: \"non disponible\" + source tentée.\nEnvoie au channel telegram topic 3 du groupe -1003791371950.\nCurrent time: Tuesday, February 10th, 2026 — 4:35 PM (UTC)\n\nReturn your summary as plain text; it will be delivered automatically. If the task explicitly calls for messaging a specific external recipient, note who/where it should go instead of sending it yourself."}],"timestamp":1770741300726}}
{"type":"message","id":"74f4937d","parentId":"b11f1223","timestamp":"2026-02-10T16:35:22.976Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Resolving messaging instructions**\n\nI need to conduct web research and possibly use web_search/web_fetch. I also need to send a message to a Telegram group. However, there's a bit of a conflict in the instructions about using the message tool. It seems like I shouldn't send the message directly myself. Instead, I might just produce a plain text summary noting where it should be sent. I should look for close prices at the EU market close after fetching multi-source data for indices and stocks.\n\n**Choosing data sources for indices**\n\nI’m looking at various sources for indices and market data. Stooq has several indices like ^FCHI, ^GDAXI, ^STOXX50E, and ^FTSE, but TradingView might be tricky if it gets blocked. For DAX data, I'd prefer Deutsche Börse, though it’s not listed. MarketWatch provides movers too, but I might want to pull from Stooq for CAC40 and DAX components to rank them. I might also need to programmatically fetch the tickers. I'll check if I can use yfinance or stick with Stooq for Michelin's ticker, which is ML.PA on Euronext Paris.\n\n**Fetching top movers and components**\n\nI believe Michelin's ticker is \"ML.PA.\" I'll evaluate it by multiplying 111 by the closing price. If I can't robustly compute the top movers, I'll mark them as \"non disponible\" and note the sources I tried. For CAC 40 components, I plan to attempt fetching data from Investing pages, possibly using web_fetch to parse the information. I’ll also use web_search to find the relevant Stooq URLs. Let's get started on that!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0593374eb0d59d6c01698b5e36050c819188928f08acbb17dd\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpi15KlU-q_qX_UwMIQcZi0SQ5efkkA4UqtWwydcMBLbcb72kYCfMitAIuTi6Oj8YAZ4ogCagFrXcj5Qs1_idVxB7io-L5j6M41iILPcKzQtFrs4MGBXKhKz8W5lvWxLk3_W03j93Ya4C-dsyHPowMEj1